| `tests.memory_scratch_min_free_mb` | integer | `4096` | a whole number of mebibytes (MiB), 0 or more | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`choose_scratch`), through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.memory_scratch_min_free_mb` row, read only when `tests.memory_scratch_root` is not null | Sets the free space the memory root's file system must have when a session starts for the session to choose it, so a host with a small memory directory, such as a container's 64 MiB, falls back to `tests.scratch_root`. Absent while `tests.memory_scratch_root` is set, or negative, it stops pytest before any test runs (exit 4), naming this key. | a limit during the run: free space is judged once, at session start | always |
